  "s12_routing_interpretation": {
    "outcome_branch": "CASE_2_SCORING_AND_ASSIGNMENT_C_PRIME_PLUS_A_PRIME",
    "rationale": "Stage B finds that lowering sim_threshold from 0.50 to 0.40 immediately improves T_TWOSTAGE_TH050 from 54.443 -> 57.572 HOTA (AssA 36.704 -> 40.845, IDF1 53.629 -> 60.117) by recovering 973 FN (5615 -> 4642) at only +46 IDSW (786 -> 832). Stage C explains both mechanisms: (1) 89.9% (134/149) of real onset switches involve spatial overlap contention IoU >= 0.30 and 74.5% (111/149) occur on consecutive gap==1 frames with assignment_margin < 0.10 (offline onset AUROC = 0.9432, 73.8% TPR at 5% FPR; 34 2-cycle swaps); (2) early unconflicted ReID anchor_reid_dist breaks S10's post-switch self-consistency trap (AUROC 0.7062 vs recent-5 0.5251 on 31,791 post-switch frames). However, Stage D falsifies write-only conflict gating as a closed-loop replacement: while G1 beats unconditional C0_TAU065 (+5.177 HOTA, 48.686 vs 43.509), all G1-G4 degrade T_TWOSTAGE_TH050 (43.380-48.686 vs 54.443) because spatial conflict occurs on ~42% of ALL mature frames (29,714/71,986 in G1), causing 4,733-7,857 write skips vs only ~82 caught onsets and starving tracklets during crowded occlusions (FN 8,055-9,759 vs 5,615). G4 early pinning further drops HOTA (44.442 -> 43.380). Consequently, Case 2 holds cleanly: write-side refusal alone cannot fix T_TWOSTAGE, routing S12 directly to association scoring & assignment reform (C' pairwise motion/occlusion bias in GAFFE + A' margin/2-cycle/deferred disambiguation, paired with calibrated TH040 regime)."
  },
